        <history>
          <p>The last of Nielsen's wind concertos, written for clarinettist Aage Oxenvad, is notable for its single continuous movement and its deliberately unstable tonal centre, reflecting what Nielsen saw as the clarinet's contradictory character — by turns warm and aggressive. A prominent snare drum part shadows the soloist throughout, creating one of the concerto repertoire's most unusual dialogues.</p>
